{"diagnosis": "Trace shows TRAP: no progress max_addr=0x00000000 with tohost FAIL 0xdead vs expected advancing fetches over 256-word NOP mem. mem_la_read at picorv32.v:380-381 never asserts so no fetch progresses. Root cause is AND (&&) joining the normal-request term and the COMPRESSED_ISA second-word term instead of OR (||), blocking all mem_la_read asserts.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picorv32.v b/picorv32.v
--- a/picorv32.v
+++ b/picorv32.v
@@ -379,4 +379,4 @@
 	assign mem_la_write = resetn && !mem_state && mem_do_wdata;
-	assign mem_la_read = resetn && ((!mem_la_use_prefetched_high_word && !mem_state && (mem_do_rinst || mem_do_prefetch || mem_do_rdata)) &&
+	assign mem_la_read = resetn && ((!mem_la_use_prefetched_high_word && !mem_state && (mem_do_rinst || mem_do_prefetch || mem_do_rdata)) ||
 			(COMPRESSED_ISA && mem_xfer && (!last_mem_valid ? mem_la_firstword : mem_la_firstword_reg) && !mem_la_secondword && &mem_rdata_latched[1:0]));
 	assign mem_la_addr = (mem_do_prefetch || mem_do_rinst) ? {next_pc[31:2] + mem_la_firstword_xfer, 2'b00} : {reg_op1[31:2], 2'b00};
", "expected": "tohost PASS (not FAIL 0xdead), no TRAP: no progress max_addr=0x00000000, max_addr advances with fetch progress"}

